# Implementation Plan - Performance & Concurrency Optimization

The goal is to resolve the 1 FPS UI degradation and high CPU usage reported on lower-spec systems by introducing CPU-aware backoff, weighting "heavy" files (Videos/RAW) more heavily in the concurrency pool, and optimizing the Diagnostics Monitor.

## Proposed Changes

### [AsyncImageProvider](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.cpp)

#### [MODIFY] [AsyncImageProvider.cpp](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.cpp)
- **CPU-Aware Admit**: Enhance [processStagedRequests](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.cpp#474-614) to check `SystemMonitor::instance()->systemCpuUsage()`. If system CPU > 85%, cut all concurrency limits by 50% or stop admitting new "Heavy" tasks.
- **Task Weighting**:
    - Implement `getTaskWeight(const QString &id)`.
    - RAW (.dng, .cr2, etc.) and Video (.mp4, .mkv, etc.) = **4 slots**.
    - Standard Images = **1 slot**.
- **Admission Logic**: Update `stats.activeTasks` to track "Active Weight" instead of simple count.

### [ScrollBenchImageModel](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp)

#### [MODIFY] [ScrollBenchImageModel.h](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.h)
- Add [Q_PROPERTY(int loadedCount READ loadedCount NOTIFY loadedCountChanged)](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.h#23-25).
- Add `m_loadedCount` member.

#### [MODIFY] [ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp)
- Increment `m_loadedCount` when a thumbnail is received and `ImageItem::isLoaded` transitions to true.
- Decrement if data is cleared.

### [DiagnosticsMonitor](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/DiagnosticsMonitor.cpp)

#### [MODIFY] [DiagnosticsMonitor.cpp](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/DiagnosticsMonitor.cpp)
- Remove the loop in [checkLoadProgress](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/DiagnosticsMonitor.cpp#131-196) that iterates over [rowCount()](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp#69-74).
- Directly use `m_model->loadedCount()`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
- **Stress Test**: Run `appScrollBench.exe --scan <path_with_heavy_files>` and observe the `[SystemMonitor]` logs.
- **Concurrency Check**: Verify that `Active Weight` (visible in logs soon) stays within the dynamic limits even when hitting many MP4s/DNGs.
- **UI FPS Check**: Observe the Diagnostics Overlay to ensure the FPS stays above 30 during heavy loading.

### Manual Verification
- Verify that the "Critical Issue: Load Stalled" warning triggers significantly less often now that we don't pin the CPU.
